// ice.koral - internal compiler error reporting
//
// A `panic` here means the COMPILER broke an invariant, not that the program
// being compiled is wrong. Those must read as such: a bare
// `Generic function symbol reached codegen: ...` looks like a user error and
// sends people debugging their own source instead of filing a bug.
//
// There is one wording, so it can be changed in one place. The detail is
// whatever identifies the broken invariant -- which symbol, which type -- and
// stays as specific as the site can make it.

/// The message for a violated compiler invariant.
///
/// Callers pass only the DETAIL; the framing is fixed here.
public let internal_compiler_error(detail String) String = {
    return "internal compiler error: \(detail)\nThis is a bug in the Koral compiler, not in the program being compiled. Please report it, along with the source that triggered it.";
};
